---
import { site } from '../site.config';
---
<header class="intro" id="top">
  <div class="wrap id">
    <div>
      <h1>{site.name}</h1>
      <p class="pron">{site.pronunciation} · he/him</p>

      <p class="lede">
        I build compilers for machine learning systems. I'm a PhD student in computer science at
        NYU's Courant Institute, advised by
        <a href="https://www.saiqianzhang.com/">Sai Qian Zhang</a>. I'm also a maintainer of
        <a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm">vLLM</a>, where I work on compilation and
        kernel fusion.
      </p>
      <p class="lede">
        My research is about giving LLM inference engines a real intermediate representation: one
        where fusion, memory reuse, and hardware portability are properties of the language rather
        than hand-written special cases. Before NYU I did my BS and MEng at MIT.
      </p>

      <div class="links">
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email</a>
        {site.links.map((l) => <a href={l.href}>{l.label}</a>)}
      </div>
    </div>
    <img class="portrait" src="/profile.jpg" alt="" width="128" height="128" />
  </div>
</header>
